;; Regulatory source register for JPN-AUDIT — the Board of Audit (会計検査院).
;;
;; README.md's core contract grounds the audit-readiness actor on the Board of
;; Audit Act (会計検査院法) and the entity's own funding/ownership facts, and
;; blueprint.edn names jbaudit.go.jp / japaneselawtranslation.go.jp /
;; hourei.ndl.go.jp as the only allowed sources. Until this file existed there
;; was no such list, so no claim in this repository could be traced to
;; anything. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository -- extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljs`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it:
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be:
;;                   laws.e-gov.go.jp answers HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>,
;;                   renders "not found" client-side, and therefore cannot
;;                   tell a real citation from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; THE HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path that
;; does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host in
;; the register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note degrades
;; into a constant the moment it is written; a declaration the run re-measures
;; cannot.
;;
;; THE TWO MEASUREMENTS THAT SHAPE THIS REGISTER (both re-measured every run):
;;
;; 1. www.jbaudit.go.jp answers **404** -- not 403, not a redirect -- for a
;;    path that does not exist, and the 404 page is a SOFT 404: 15471 bytes of
;;    real site chrome whose <title> is the SITE title ("会計検査院 Board of
;;    Audit of Japan"), identical to the front page's title. On this host a
;;    title alone separates nothing; only the status does. 404 is not 2xx, so
;;    the :page-identity status check still discriminates -- but a checker
;;    written to look for 403 (the refusal the sibling METI hosts give) would
;;    misread this host as blocked. The status is pinned in
;;    :host/missing-status and compared on every run.
;;
;; 2. www.jbaudit.go.jp does NOT redirect http:// to https://: the http form
;;    of a real page answers 404 at the http URL. The redirect self-test in
;;    verify-facts.cljs is therefore aimed at the OTHER host in the register
;;    (www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp, which does redirect), and the
;;    self-test walks the pool and requires SOME host to demonstrate the
;;    redirect branch rather than assuming every host behaves the same.
;;
;; Claims stop at the level actually checked -- law identity via the API, and
;; for the pages the title, the URL, the charset and the strings read on
;; 2026-08-30. No article text and no PDF is asserted, because none was read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.www-jbaudit-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.jbaudit.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "会計検査院 itself. A nonexistent path answers 404 with a
                15471-byte soft-404 page served at the requested URL, whose
                <title> is the SITE title -- identical to the front page's
                title, so on this host the title separates nothing and the
                status is the only discriminator. Also measured: the host does
                NOT redirect http:// to https:// -- the http form of a real
                page answers 404 at the http URL. No challenge has been
                observed on this host; if one appears, this entity is the
                first thing to re-measure."}

 {:source/id "host.www-japaneselawtranslation-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "法務省の日本法令外国語訳DB (Ministry of Justice Japanese Law
                Translation database). A nonexistent path answers 404 with a
                short \"Error - Japanese Law Translation\" page -- unlike the
                Board of Audit host, the title DOES separate the error page
                from real pages here. This host DOES redirect http:// to
                https://, which is what the verifier's redirect self-test
                exercises. The translation is explicitly NOT an official
                text; this register cites it as the Ministry of Justice's
                published English rendering of the statute, never as the
                statute itself."}

